<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>REMUS-100</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>

  <description>
    Real US Navy shallow-water mine-countermeasures AUV, and the most-cited
    AUV in academic hydrodynamics literature. Mass/dimensions/inertia/drag
    sourced from Thor I. Fossen's MIT-licensed PythonVehicleSimulator
    reference implementation (github.com/cybergalactic/PythonVehicleSimulator).

    IMPORTANT: this twin's actuation is a 6-thruster vectored frame (the
    same proven architecture BlueROV2 uses on ArduSub), NOT the real
    vehicle's actual propeller-plus-two-fins control scheme. No ArduPilot
    firmware currently supports fin-steered AUV control -- see model.sdf's
    header comment for the full investigation (including a genuine attempt
    via ArduPlane firmware that hit a firmware-level dead end). Hull
    physics (mass, buoyancy, dimensions, drag) are real and sourced;
    actuator layout is a disclosed simplification.

    Properties (sourced)

    Length:    1.6 m
    Diameter:  0.19 m
    Mass:      31.9 kg (neutrally buoyant)

    ArduPilot

    Vehicle type: Sub
    Frame:        6-thruster vectored (ArduSub default, same as BlueROV2)
  </description>
</model>
